It completed the sprint at 9.776s and state results. But player dist 119? After finish p.dist=100, then update continues? Wait we removed state='finished', so update keeps running after p.finished, and p.dist += speed*dt because the `if (p.started)` block still runs each frame, even after finished. It sets p.dist to 100 when crossing, but continues to accumulate beyond 100 until done. That's a bug: athlete will run past 100 while waiting for AI, and camera follows p.dist beyond finish. It also might draw player beyond finish line. Need to stop player movement when finished. In `update`, wrap movement only if !p.finished. Since p.finished true after line, skip position increments and keep dist=100. Also AI stop at 100. Let's patch:
```
if (p.started && !p.finished) { ... }
```
But then p.speed remains whatever; set p.speed *= exp maybe? For pose, after finished we want him decelerating. In render, `if (r.finished && r.speed<1.5) pose='idle'`. p.speed stays high, so he keeps running in place at finish. Set p.speed *= exp(-2.2*dt) when finished. Also update p.phase to slow? Fine.

Also the finishDelay logic:
```
if (p.finished && (allDone || this.finishDelay > 1.35)) {
  this.finishDelay += dt;
  if (this.finishDelay > 1.35) { done }
}
```
The condition `this.finishDelay > 1.35` is inside the outer condition and initially false, so it only ever begins if allDone. Then finishDelay increments and after 1.35s done. So if some AI never finish, allDone false and finishDelay stays 0, never done. But all AI finish eventually (unless targetTime slow). Actually outer condition `p.finished && (allDone || this.finishDelay > 1.35)`; when not allDone and finishDelay 0, false, so finishDelay never increments. So the timeout never starts. Should simply be:
```
if (p.finished) {
  this.finishDelay += dt;
  if (allDone || this.finishDelay > 1.35) { done }
}
```
Fix that.

Also the camera after player finishes: updateCamera follows p.dist=100 and view shifts to finish. Good.

Let's patch sprint.

Also player result 9.776 is good.

Now look at the results screen screenshot. But first fix.

Additionally, the auto-run fallback lets idle player finish ~? At speed 5.1, 100m takes ~20s. The results at 11.55s race time because autopilot tapped. Good.

Let's patch dt clamp and sprint update.

