content.text:
Now CSS for tablet controls. Add after the responsive section or before. We'll add a dedicated section at the end before prefers-reduced-motion maybe. Use body.is-touch + min-width:821px.

Need to carefully override:
```
@media (min-width:821px){
  body.is-touch .touch-controls{display:flex}
  body.is-touch .action-controls{display:flex}
  body.is-touch .key-hints{display:none}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-sprint .action-controls{display:none!important}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-field .touch-controls{display:none!important}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-javelin .touch-controls{display:none!important}
  body.is-touch .hud-icon-btn{width:42px;height:42px}
  body.is-touch .hud-prompt{bottom:calc(154px + var(--safe-bottom));}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-javelin .hud-prompt{bottom:calc(200px + var(--safe-bottom))}
  body.is-touch .touch-controls{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;margin:0;padding:0 38px;transform:none;justify-content:space-between;pointer-events:none}
  body.is-touch .tap-btn{width:88px;height:88px;pointer-events:auto}
  body.is-touch .tap-btn span{font-size:32px}
  body.is-touch .cadence-orbit{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:42px;transform:translateX(-50%);flex-direction:row;width:auto;gap:9px}
  body.is-touch .cadence-orbit i{width:6px;height:6px}
  body.is-touch .cadence-orbit i:nth-child(2){width:8px;height:8px}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-sprint .meter-cluster{position:absolute;left:38px;bottom:120px;width:210px}
  body.is-touch .action-controls{position:absolute;right:40px;bottom:24px;padding:0}
  body.is-touch .action-btn{width:112px;height:112px}
  body.is-touch .action-btn span{font-size:29px}
  body.is-touch .javelin-cluster{position:absolute;right:32px;bottom:16px;margin:0}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-javelin .action-controls{right:238px;bottom:38px}
  body.is-touch .hud.is-javelin .action-btn{width:100px;height:100px}
  body.is-touch .prompt-key.is-tap{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.05em}
}
```
Wait `.hud-prompt` bottom at 154px relative to HUD screen. The sprint pads are 88px tall at bottom ~24 → top 112, so prompt at 154 clears. The meter at bottom 120 + 24 = 144; prompt at 154 clears by 10. Good. For field, action button 112 at bottom 24 → top 136; prompt at 154 clears. Javelin dial 150 at bottom 16 → top 166; prompt at 200. Good.

But the prompt is centered; on tablet it may overlap the meter's top? No, meter left, prompt center.

The meter for sprint at bottom 120 (relative to hud-bottom, bottom 24) actually 144 from screen; the prompt at 154 (above by 10). The meter height ~60, from 144 to 204. The prompt at 154 overlaps the meter's vertical band but horizontally the prompt is centered and meter at left 38 width 210 → ends 248; prompt centered width ~300 on 1024 → starts 362. No overlap. Fine.

But setting `.meter-cluster{position:absolute}` removes it from flow; the `.hud-bottom` height may collapse to 0 (if action-controls/touch absolute and javelin absolute). Then the absolute children's containing block has height 0 at bottom 24; the touch controls bottom 0 => at 24. Fine. The action controls bottom 24px relative to hud-bottom (height 0) => 24+24 = 48 from screen bottom. Fine. The javelin cluster bottom 16 => 40. Fine. That's okay, but mixing. Actually `.hud-bottom` is positioned with `bottom:calc(24px+safe)` and no explicit height; if all children absolute, height 0. Absolute children with bottom values place relative to the padding box (height 0) at that bottom. So `.action-controls{bottom:24px}` → 48px above screen bottom. Good.

But touch-controls left/right 0 spans the full width of `.hud-bottom` padding box, which is full width minus its own padding (0 clamp(16,2.6vw,40)). It has padding 0 38px, so pads at 38px from edges of the hud-bottom content box, which itself is inset 40px → 78px from screen edges. Maybe too inset. Set hud-bottom padding? In tablet query:
```
body.is-touch .hud-bottom{padding:0;bottom:calc(16px+safe)}
```
Then touch controls span full width with 34px padding → pads 34px from edges. Meter left 38. Good. But for field action right 40.

Let's set `.hud-bottom{padding:0; bottom:calc(16px+safe)}`. Then positions relative to height 0 at 16px bottom:
- touch bottom 0 → 16px
- tap 88 → top 104; prompt 154 good.
- meter bottom 120 → 136; top 196.
- action bottom 24 → 40; top 152; prompt 154 nearly touches. Set prompt 176 for field maybe. Let's use 172.
- javelin cluster bottom 16 → 32; top 182; prompt 204.
- javelin action right 238 bottom 38 → 54; top 166.

Prompt bottom 176 clears action top 152 and meter top 196? Prompt 176 bottom, height 50 → 176-226 from bottom. Meter 136-196 from bottom: prompt overlaps vertically 176-196 and horizontally? meter left 38-248; prompt center starts ~350; no overlap. Fine.

For sprint prompt 176: meter 136-196, no overlap. Fine. Use 176 for all, 210 for javelin.

But on a tablet, the HUD top and mini board take up space. Prompt at 176 from bottom is fine.

Also, the javelin dial's `angle-read` bottom 16 inside the 150px cluster; fine.

The action button in javelin: shows THROW / TAP HERE. Good.

Need to make sure `.touch-controls` doesn't overlap the meter for sprint: L pad left 34, width 88; meter left 38 width 210 at bottom 136-196. Pads at bottom 16-104. No vertical overlap. Good.

Also adjust tap buttons to be nearer the bottom corners: 34px from edges, 16px bottom. Good for thumbs. On a tablet 1024x768, the bottom corners are reachable.

One more: the `.hud-prompt` might overlap the mini board on tablet? No, mini board is top-left.

Now add CSS.

